### Weather Images API
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and Visual Studio / Rider .http support.
# Flow: POST /api/jobs -> poll GET /api/jobs/{id} until status = "completed" -> open the image links.
# The job endpoints need the API key in the x-api-key header. The key is shared separately, not in this repo.

@baseUrl = https://weather-func-bqurxt3tu2lka.kindhill-bfd226d6.italynorth.azurecontainerapps.io
@apiKey = PASTE_API_KEY_HERE
# Local: func start in ./src (API_KEY in local.settings.json)
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:7071

### Health check (no key needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Ping

### Start a new image job -> 202 Accepted { jobId, statusUrl }
# @name startJob
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Job status: "queued" -> "processing" (imagesCompleted/stationCount) -> "completed" with image links in "images"
# Image links are read-only SAS URLs valid for 24 hours; calling this again issues fresh ones.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/{{startJob.response.body.jobId}}
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### Without the key -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs

### Unknown job id -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/00000000000000000000000000000000
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
